      "side": 1,
      "message": "THe file represents artificial type dependencies. `struct task` is there because of some register magic on some architectures (including ARM64, I suppose). The module structure is there is because it is used by the module loader and must remain stable for load-link to actually work.\n\nBoth symbols could be called \"paranoia\" and there may be other symbols in the ABI that would pull them in anyway. It doesn\u0027t hurt to keep them.",
      "parentUuid": "61d6550b_1779e4cc",
      "revId": "ca53fea695c54973b46a115f6f87bf0e5a0d6036",
