      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T14:28:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I discussed this in more detail with @umendez@google.com.\n\nFor GKI, the base symbol list is like a synthetic module dependency. The question is then: is it a GKI module or a vendor module?\n\n* vendor module - this is the easiest and simplest interpretation, the symbols are available to vendors, they are in the ABI and so stability is guaranteed\n* GKI module - doesn\u0027t really make sense, we need these symbols to be ABI stable\n\nIt seems quite odd to put something in a symbol list and the ABI and then not allow it to be used. This is what this change is fixing.\n\n---\n\nThe symbols cannot be used for any mischief.",
